# Security policy (agents)

Root [`SECURITY.md`](SECURITY.md) is the canonical vulnerability-reporting policy
(GitHub Security tab). Do not invent alternate public channels in docs or issues.

## When you must update `SECURITY.md`

Update it (same PR when practical) if the change affects any of:

- How to report vulns (private advisory URL, contact, disclosure expectations)
- Supported versions / prerelease support stance
- **In scope / out of scope** trust boundaries (IPC, wipe/import/move path safety,
  credential storage, installer signing, Electron fuses, allowlisted browser opens)
- Known documented limits that are explicitly called out as out-of-scope
  (e.g. DPAPI [#144], Authenticode [#142]) when those issues close or the product
  behavior changes

## Keep related operator docs in sync

| Surface | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `SECURITY.md` | Researcher / reporter policy |
| `website/.../security-privacy.mdx` | Operator storage, network, secrets hygiene |
| `README.md` Security section | Short pointer + high-level boundary |
| `docs/versioning.md` | Packaged fuses / release trust |

When you change credential storage, installer trust, or packaged hardening, update
the matching rows above so they do not contradict each other. Prefer one short
cross-link over duplicating long prose.

## Do not

- File or suggest **public** GitHub issues for security vulns
- Paste exploit PoCs into public PR descriptions
- Claim DPAPI, Authenticode, or encryption that the product does not ship yet
